.TH SMDRAW 1
.SH NAME
smdraw \- make the drawing of a part
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B smdraw
.I part.draw part.st
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Smdraw
makes the PostScript drawing of a part, or of the parts of an
assembly in place, as described by its drawing file,
.IR draw (5).
Each view is projected by
.IR smview (1),
its curves within .001 in on the paper at the largest scale it may
take (its own, that of the scale record, or 2),
and dimensioned by
.IR smdim (1)
at its scale, in the units of the drawing, with the indented records
under it, as
.B smsheet \-v
lists them;
the views are then laid on the sheets by
.IR smsheet (1).
Without a scale record, the views are made at the scales
2, 1.5, 1, .75, .5, .375 and .25, from the largest the paper can hold,
until every sheet has a scale.
The programs are taken from the directory of the script, or from
$PLICAD_BIN if set.
.SH EXAMPLES
smdraw part.draw part.st >part.ps
.br
ps2pdf \-sFONTPATH=$PLICAD/lib/fonts part.ps part.pdf
.SH SEE ALSO
draw(5), smview(1), smdim(1), smsheet(1), ps2pdf(1)
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
FILE:LINE: and the fault, from any program of the pipe.
